Author: Arijit Roy <royarijit1995@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 25 15:09:24 2026 +0530

    fix(runs): review follow-ups — alert builder on the as-of snapshot, later_version marker, one CheckAsOfRead, honest unknown-check payload (#1613)

    - alerting/builder.py read expectation_type and the redaction column from the LIVE check and
      made two check_versions reads; it now takes the same `historical_check_snapshots` as REST/MCP.
    - `resolved_from` gains `later_version` for the clock-skew branch (every version postdates the
      result, the earliest stands in) instead of calling that `version`.
    - `ResultCheckRead` collapsed into one `CheckAsOfRead` used by results and comparison sides.
    - MCP: the three derived dicts are gone (direct `as_of[r.id]`), `engine` is null for an unknown
      check instead of a fabricated `gx`, docstrings name all four states.
    - run_comparison.CheckIdentity.resolved_from uses the shared Literal.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

